<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Timur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1336">1336</a>–<a href="/years/1405">1405</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Tamerlane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Timur, also known as Tamerlane, was a Turco-Mongol conqueror who rose to power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> in the late fourteenth century and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>. His campaigns stretched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-delhi-1398">sack of Delhi</a> in 1398, and were marked by extreme brutality. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> his capital, and his descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> later founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/timur.jpg" alt="Timur" width="278" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: shakko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timur_reconstruction03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
